WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
It is desired to use a crane to deposit an HVAC system onto a roof.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.900
The crane is mounted on building B, as shown, and is intended to deposit its load onto

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.000
building A.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.800
A tree stands in between buildings A and B, and its height prevents the crane from lowering

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.559
its boom arm below 50 degrees.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:28.800
If the crane wishes to deposit the HVAC system, at least 20 feet away from the edge of the

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:35.160
building A roof, how long does the boom arm need to be in feet?

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.320
So this problem is all geometry.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.159
We are looking for the length of the boom arm here, and given the other information we have

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:47.159
in blue, we can solve for that pretty quickly.

00:00:47.159 --> 00:00:54.480
The problem also notes that the boom arm is restricted to being lowered to 50 degrees at most.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.480
So if we were to draw this out really quickly, this could be our

00:00:58.479 --> 00:01:01.599
conceptual step one.

00:01:01.599 --> 00:01:06.599
We have X is what we're trying to solve for right now.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:12.159
We have the distance.

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:23.519
We have the degrees that we've been given.

00:01:23.519 --> 00:01:32.039
And we need to know that we need to cross a span of here to here, and also here to here.

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:38.439
So if we sum up 75 and 20 on the bottom, we don't even need the additional information about

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:46.439
the height of the building, and we don't need to compare the heights over here to the

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.799
height of this building.

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:52.799
We have enough information to solve this very quickly.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:59.359
So rearranging the triangle, we can say that the cosine of the hypotenuse or the boom arm

00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:10.000
is going to be equal to the adjacent over the hypotenuse.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:17.039
So filling those in, we have a cosine of 50 degrees equals 95 over the hypotenuse.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:32.800
Solving for that, the hypotenuse is going to be equal to 95 divided by the cosine of 50.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.800
And this is going to be 147.5 feet.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.800
This would make our closest answer over here 150.
